## Circuit Connections

The following table shows the ESP32 pin connections for the Machine Vibration Frequency Analysis project.

| S.No. | Component | Component Pin | ESP32 GPIO Pin |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Acoustic Emission (AE) Sensor | Analog Output | GPIO 34 |
| 2 | AE Sensor | GND | GND |
| 3 | AE Sensor | VCC | According to module specifications |
| 4 | Ultrasonic Receiver | Analog Output | GPIO 35 |
| 5 | Ultrasonic Receiver | GND | GND |
| 6 | Ultrasonic Receiver | VCC | According to module specifications |
| 7 | 16×2 I2C LCD | SDA | GPIO 25 |
| 8 | 16×2 I2C LCD | SCL | GPIO 26 |
| 9 | I2C LCD | VCC | Compatible supply voltage |
| 10 | I2C LCD | GND | GND |
| 11 | Green LED | Anode (+) through resistor | GPIO 18 |
| 12 | Yellow LED | Anode (+) through resistor | GPIO 19 |
| 13 | Red LED | Anode (+) through resistor | GPIO 21 |
| 14 | All LEDs | Cathode (-) | GND |
| 15 | Buzzer | Positive (+) | GPIO 22 |
| 16 | Buzzer | Negative (-) | GND |
| 17 | ESP32 | USB | Computer or suitable USB power source |

### Connection Notes

- Use a 220–330 Ω current-limiting resistor for each LED.
- Connect all circuit grounds together where required by the sensor interface.
- Check the sensor output voltage before connecting it to the ESP32 ADC pins.
- Use suitable amplification, filtering, and protection circuits for the AE sensor and ultrasonic receiver as required.
- Verify the LCD's supply voltage and I2C logic-level compatibility.
- The sensor power and signal connections depend on the exact sensor modules used.
